From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bpereira <bpereira@cloudflare.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 22:05:40 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Rebuild derived state instead of storing it

Rebuild table cells' grid styles instead of storing them: cells keep their computed
style and grid placement and rebuild the taffy style with the same conversion on
each read, while captions, whose margins point into the table's adjustments, keep
theirs.

Shape outside list markers when painted instead of keeping them: items record the
scale and paint shapes the marker from the item's style with the contexts that
rebuild evicted text. Paint output is unchanged.

Box scroll and pin offsets only for boxes that have them: one box allocated on the
first nonzero write shrinks LayoutData from 248 to 232 bytes on wasm32.

Key the id map by atom instead of a copied string, sharing the atom elements
already intern.

Reserve initial paint-child buffers to their contributor bound, avoiding
minimum-four padding on first allocation while keeping amortized growth for buffers
already allocated.
